  "limit_case_specification": {
    "construction_policy": "These finite declarative fixture specifications construct data only, never executable source. The test author may materialize repeated scalar strings, records or byte padding using the explicit counts below. Expected outcomes are literal and must not be computed by the implementation-under-test. Record constructors use the literal templates in this document, compact UTF-8 JSON and LF framing unless a case explicitly removes LF. Boundary counts include the initial session_meta. Large limit data need not be stored in this oracle.",
    "cases": [
